@ [dual_hemisphere] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Cantor_Runtime_Procedure_FPGA_Dual_Hemisphere_Review_2026-08-05.sop

& [Claim_CPPE_01] recurring inference-control patterns deserve executable semantic identity
  + [support] repeated prose prompting is difficult to version, validate, replay, revoke, and compare
  + [counterargument] ordinary tool functions and prompts are sufficient
  + [answer] use procedures only where process state, reuse, SOP anchors, negotiation, replay, or governance add measurable value
  + [confidence] is medium_high
  + [invalidation] experiments show no reliability or audit advantage over ordinary typed functions

& [Claim_CPPE_02] Simula is a useful semantic ancestor but not the implementation language
  + [support] durable process identity, event ordering, passivation, reactivation, and quasi-parallel sequencing map directly to explicit procedure states
  + [counterargument] adopting the name imports obsolete syntax and runtime assumptions
  + [answer] only mapped semantics survive; vintage syntax, inheritance, allocation, and compatibility are explicit non-goals
  + [confidence] is high
  + [invalidation] the mapped concepts produce no simpler or more precise procedure semantics than a conventional state machine vocabulary

& [Claim_CPPE_03] canonical typed IR should be the portability waist
  + [support] source syntax, model provider, interpreter, WASM, native software, and hardware layouts can vary while semantic trace remains stable
  + [counterargument] a new IR creates compiler complexity and premature lock-in
  + [answer] the first IR is deliberately small, versioned, exact-only, and may be revised through explicit migration
  + [confidence] is medium_high
  + [invalidation] two representative bounded procedures cannot be expressed without unsafe escape hatches or backend-specific semantics

& [Claim_CPPE_04] proposal through invocation must be separate phases
  + [support] model-generated source is untrusted input and each phase answers a different question
  + [counterargument] many development systems compile and run in one command
  + [answer] the extra ceremony is reserved for admitted reusable inference procedures whose identity and authority persist beyond one response
  + [confidence] is high
  + [invalidation] phase separation cannot prevent any material fault or authority confusion in the experiment

& [Claim_CPPE_05] serialized continuations are preferable to native coroutine stacks
  + [support] they are inspectable, portable, versionable, replayable, and independently validated
  + [counterargument] native coroutines are simpler and faster
  + [answer] reference correctness and portability precede optimization; later backends can optimize while proving semantic correspondence
  + [confidence] is high
  + [invalidation] required process behavior cannot be represented without opaque runtime state

& [Claim_CPPE_06] shared inference should be explicit message coordination
  + [support] separate models do not naturally share hidden state and explicit records preserve identity, causality, evidence, and version
  + [counterargument] multiple tool turns are slower and may lose the fluidity of joint reasoning
  + [answer] the protocol trades some latency for inspectability; batching and acceleration remain later measured optimizations
  + [confidence] is high
  + [invalidation] measured multi-pass quality and utility are consistently worse than independent outputs plus simple synthesis

& [Claim_CPPE_07] token-ring stability is a useful bounded experiment, not a truth mechanism
  + [support] it provides an exact termination rule for unchanged negotiated state across named participants
  + [counterargument] participants can converge on error or keep changing forever
  + [answer] objections, qualifications, budgets, timeout, refusal, and Observer review remain explicit; convergence is only stability evidence
  + [confidence] is medium
  + [invalidation] the rule rewards empty agreement or cannot terminate on representative tasks

& [Claim_CPPE_08] the first procedure profile must be effectless
  + [support] this isolates types, state, scheduling, compilation, admission, invocation, and replay from external authority and compensation
  + [counterargument] an effectless assistant procedure cannot do useful work
  + [answer] it can retrieve supplied anchors, transform typed data, deliberate, validate, plan, score, route, and emit proposals; effects can follow separate proof
  + [confidence] is high
  + [invalidation] no meaningful representative use case can be completed without a live effect

& [Claim_CPPE_09] hand-authored and model-shaped candidates must share one pipeline
  + [support] model authorship must not receive a privileged parser, validator, verifier, or admission route
  + [counterargument] generated source may need error-tolerant normalization
  + [answer] a model may repair a rejected candidate in another turn, but the admitted pipeline remains identical
  + [confidence] is high
  + [invalidation] equal treatment prevents faithful source attribution or secure isolation

& [Claim_CPPE_10] model tool calling is sufficient for the first inference seam
  + [support] structured request, external execution, structured result, and later inference already express the required causal boundary
  + [counterargument] it is not interaction inside one transformer forward pass
  + [answer] that limitation is stated honestly; the intended portable semantic state exists outside hidden activations
  + [confidence] is high
  + [invalidation] a required use case proves impossible without engine-level interruption finer than the structured tool boundary

& [JustificationDisposition] is accepted_for_canonical_authoring
  + the experiment is justified as bounded infrastructure research, not as a claim of a new general-purpose language model
